    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20239" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βόθρ-ος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hole, trench</i>, or <i>pit dug
				in the ground</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βόθρον ὀρύξαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					10.517
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βόθρου τ᾽ ἐξέστρεψε [τὴν
			ἐλαίαν</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				17.58
			</span></i>; <i>trough</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				6.92
			</span></i>: generally, <i>hollow</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				4.5.6
			</span></i>; <i>grave,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				14.238
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Aerae</span>); ritual <i>pit</i> for
			offerings to 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποχθόνιοι θεοί, β. καὶ μέγαρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Antr.</u>
					6
				</span></i>
			.</div>
